# School Schedule (Linux)

A Linux re-creation of the macOS menu-bar app *School Schedule 1.0*, rebuilt from the
behaviour visible in its binary (the original source was not available).

Lives in the **system tray**. Click the icon for a panel showing the current class, a live
countdown, today's periods, after-school events and homework.

## Features
- Bell schedules: regular / short / advisory, with day-type picked automatically
- Rotation days (A/B, 6-day drop, etc.) anchored to a date, skipping weekends and days off
- Days off / breaks, last day of school, optional lunch waves
- Classes with colours and a per-rotation-day plan grid; 3 starter templates
- Homework (due "next class", tomorrow or a date), weekly after-school events
- Notifications: class-start, morning summary, evening homework (via `notify-send`)
- Tray icon shows minutes left; themes + custom accent; launch at login (XDG autostart)
- Data in `~/.config/school-schedule/data.json` (export/import in Settings)

## Run
    ./install.sh
    school-schedule              # start (or show the panel if already running)
    school-schedule --toggle     # toggle panel   (bind this to a key)
    school-schedule --settings | --show | --quit

### Hyprland / Wayland
Wayland apps can't place themselves, so the panel is moved to the top-right by default; add
a rule if you want it elsewhere, e.g. `windowrulev2 = float, title:^(School Schedule)$`, and
bind `school-schedule --toggle`. Waybar needs its `tray` module for the icon.
